WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Drop an ice cube into a glass of water.

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.650
It bobs straight back up and floats.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:12.630
Out on a frozen lake it's the same story: a lid of ice on top, with liquid water underneath.

00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:16.450
Ice and water are the same substance, the same molecules.

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.890
So why does the solid sit on top of its own liquid?

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:21.790
Why does ice float?

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:29.850
In this mission, you'll put liquid water and ice side by side, and work out what actually changes when water freezes.

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:37.990
You'll follow a lake as it cools through autumn into winter, and find out why it freezes from the top, and what would happen if it didn't.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: explain why ice floats.
